{% doc %}
  The returns position, in one line, before purchase.

  HANDOFF.md leaves the exchange policy open and instructs: "build the
  returns line as a single Liquid include so one edit changes the product
  page, the FAQ and the confirmation page together." This is that include.
  Nothing else in the theme may state the returns position in its own words.

  ── Which line renders ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  `shop.metafields.custom.returns_mode` chooses. The field does not exist on
  the live store yet; absent, this renders the CLAIMS-ONLY line, which is
  what the published Refund Policy actually says today. Create the metafield
  and set it to `exchange` on the day Option B is adopted — the product page,
  and every other surface rendering this snippet, change together.

      (absent) | claims  → Option A, CONTENT.md §09 — no size returns
      exchange            → Option B, CONTENT.md §09 — size exchange only

  ── Why the wording here is not CONTENT.md's verbatim ─────────────────
  CONTENT.md §09 Option A says a 48-hour claim window. The PUBLISHED refund
  policy on the live store says 24 hours and additionally requires a
  continuous unboxing video for every claim. The published policy is the one
  in force, so it wins; a product page promising 48 hours would contradict
  the document a customer is held to. Flagged in ADMIN-TODO — if 48 hours is
  the intended figure, the policy page is what needs correcting, then this.

  @param {string} [class] - extra classes on the wrapper
  @param {boolean} [show_label] - render the "Returns" label. Default false.

  @example
  {% render 'sv-returns-line', class: 'sv-pdp__fact', show_label: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign mode = shop.metafields.custom.returns_mode.value
-%}

<div class="sv-returns {{ class }}">
  {%- if show_label -%}
    <span class="lab lab--grey sv-returns__lab">Returns</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if mode == 'exchange' -%}
    <p class="sv-returns__body">
      <strong>Wrong size? Send it back within 7 days and we&rsquo;ll swap it.</strong>
      Same design, different size, unworn and with tags on. You cover the return
      postage; we cover sending the replacement. We do not refund for change of
      mind. If your order arrives damaged, incorrect or incomplete, message us
      within 24 hours with your unboxing video and we replace it and pay the
      postage both ways.
    </p>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="sv-returns__body">
      <strong>We do not accept size or change-of-mind returns</strong> &mdash; which is
      why this garment&rsquo;s measurements are on this page rather than in a chart
      somewhere else. If it arrives damaged, incorrect or incomplete, message us
      within 24 hours with your unboxing video and we replace it or refund it in
      full, and we pay the postage.
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* The reading pass (sv-system.css §03c). This is a paragraph someone reads
     before spending money, so it takes ink at regular weight, not the warm
     grey 300 that [data-sv] p ships for campaign surfaces. Compound selector
     because that rule is (0,1,1). */
  [data-sv] .sv-returns__body {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.66;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-returns__body strong {
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .sv-returns__lab {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.7em;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
